    "description": "Tracer! Lightbox tracing app is an integrated tracing app for drawing and illustrating. This app is meant to be used with a physical paper for stencilling and drawing. you just need to select a template picture, then place a tracing paper over it and begin tracing.\r\n\r\nThe default app is a white screen with a brightness control setting. Place your reference picture over the device and begin tracing. Great for tracing drawings and fonts, making stencils, colouring sheets, connect-the-dot's puzzles, etc.\r\n\r\nYou use the app to search for image references from the internet (using keywords or URL links), or an image from the device storage, or take a photo from the camera. Then place a tracing paper over the image and begin copying.\r\n\r\nThere is a lock button which will maximize the drawing space, and prevent the device from sleeping.\r\n\r\n It's really great for making stencils and to practice drawing with.\r\n\r\nFeatures include: -\r\n\r\n- a handy color adjust to change the gray-scale of the picture for better tracing contrasts.\r\n- pan, rotate, zoom the drawing references. \r\n- button to toggle rotate on and off \r\n- buttons to save and share the drawing references for the future.\r\n\r\nThe app is suitable for artists, students as well as casual users including retirees to do art and craft.\r\n\r\nThere is a wide range of uses for Tracer! app including: -\r\n- traditional cell art animation and tracing\r\n- calligraphy and font tracing (e.g. to transfer calligraphic fonts and swirl patterns onto posters and paintings)\r\n- making stencils  (e.g. for Halloween pumpkin carving; graffiti and spray painting art; Christmas snow stencils; cake decorating stencils)\r\n- tracing tattoo designs and patterns  \r\n- base template (e.g. underlay basic perspectives for drawing architectural structures like buildings; \r\nunderlay simple shapes to draw more complicated art pieces)",
